  "notes": "Cash basis; beginning/ending cash = total governmental funds fund balance (cash) per p4/p3. Main statement (p4) Total Governmental Funds column used; interfund transfers (and a reclassification column) net to zero in the total column, so no transfers are shown at top level. Debt Services disbursement 778,058 split into principal 470,000 and interest/fees 308,058 (307,258 + 800) using the Bond Fund schedule. Other Local Receipts 709,699 includes activities fund receipts and nutrition sales; mapped to charges for services/fees. Detail: General fund schedules (p5-6), Depreciation, Employee Benefit, School Nutrition, Bond, Building and Student Fee funds recorded; Activities Fund schedule (p13, by student club) not itemized (totals receipts 392,825 incl. 278 interest, disbursements 385,227). Interfund transfers are in 'other financing' in detail (General transfer out shown negative); printed fund totals (e.g. General receipts 8,808,248 do not include transfers; General disbursements 8,272,212 and Depreciation receipts 128,578, Nutrition receipts 458,666 do include transfers) so detail_totals for those equal the sum of the itemized revenue/expenditure lines excluding transfers (General expenditure 8,197,212; Depreciation revenue 28,578; Nutrition revenue 383,666). School expenditure schedules show function only, so detail_category for most is miscellaneous expenditure or best-fit object where the line name states it. Employee Benefit fund has no revenue other than the transfer from General. Zero-dash lines omitted. Original budget given only as Orig/Final combined and only recorded where the schedule printed it for small funds; General fund budget totals were 8,356,580 receipts / 9,098,662 disbursements (not itemized)."
